# The .claude/ deploy tree is a disposable build artifact regenerated from the
# source store in agent-system/extensions/ (selection pinned by the project-root
# .claude-extensions.json). Nothing under it is hand-authored — every deployed
# file has a source, enforced by the check-extension-docs.sh hard gate — so it is
# not tracked. Wipe and regenerate from the <leader>al picker at any time.
/.claude/
# Runtime logs relocated out of .claude/.opencode so they survive a wipe (see
# agent-system/extensions/core/docs/architecture/extension-system.md)
**/.agent-logs/
# Staging directory for the settings.json/settings.local.json backup/restore
# wrapper (settings_backup.lua) used across a full .claude/.opencode wipe.
/.claude-settings-backup/
/.opencode-settings-backup/
/specs/tmp
# /.claude/tmp/ is covered by the blanket /.claude/ rule above
/.opencode/tmp/
**/.postflight-pending
**/.git-snapshot-marker
# git-snapshot.sh --no-revert mode's untracked-file backup: ignoring it keeps a later
# `git stash -u` and `git clean -fd` from removing it, keeps task-scoped staging from
# committing it, and keeps `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` from nesting
# backups of backups on repeat runs.
**/untracked-backup-*/
# Ephemeral orchestrator runtime state: per-dispatch scratch, mutex directories, and loop
# guards. Ignored because none of these have a freshness gate on read — a git-restored copy
# would silently corrupt in-flight cycle/churn state (see
# .claude/context/standards/orchestrator-runtime-files.md for the full two-class policy and the
# freshness-gate rationale). Deliberately does NOT include .orchestrator-handoff.json or the
# bare .return-meta.json — those are durable, freshness-gated provenance and MUST stay tracked;
# see that same standard's "Untracking Already-Committed Ephemeral Files" section before ever
# adding either back here.
**/.lock/
**/.dispatch/
**/.orchestrator-loop-guard
**/.continuation-loop-guard
**/.orchestrator-churn-state.json
**/.postflight-loop-guard
**/.orchestrator-multi-state*.json
**/.drift-inspection.json
**/.return-meta-*.json
# Archived copies of the two ephemeral files above, written by the loop-guard-staleness
# detector (hard mode only) and the budget-continuation override (both modes) before
# reinitializing at cycle_count=0 / total_churn=0. Same freshness-gate rationale as the live
# files they archive.
**/.stale-loop-guard-*.json
**/.stale-churn-state-*.json
**/.exhausted-loop-guard-*.json
**/.events.lock
**/.errors.lock
**/.commit-lock/
**/.deploy-lock/
**/.scope-lock/
**/.sessions/
**/.freshness-warn-streak.json
# Durable redeploy ledger (specs/.orchestrator-deploy-ledger.json by default): a machine-local,
# cross-invocation record, distinct in KIND from every other pattern in this block above. It is
# gitignored not because it is disposable per-cycle scratch, but because it describes THIS
# machine's own .claude/ deploy state and would mislead if committed and read on another clone.
# Every read is hash-gated (see agent-system/extensions/core/scripts/lib/deploy-ledger-lib.sh),
# so a stale or git-restored copy can only ever trigger an extra redeploy, never a wrong skip.
# See .claude/context/standards/orchestrator-runtime-files.md's Class Table for the full note.
**/.orchestrator-deploy-ledger.json
# Note: specs/events.jsonl and specs/errors.json are deliberately NOT ignored — they are
# durable stores (see .claude/context/formats/events-format.md and errors-format.md). Do not
# add either here.
.syncprotect
specs/literature/**/*.pdf
specs/literature/**/*.djvu
# Literature SQLite databases (ephemeral - rebuilt from chunk files)
.literature.db
.literature.db.tmp
specs/literature/.literature.db
specs/literature/.literature.db.tmp
# (.claude/scripts/literature-pyenv/ is covered by the blanket /.claude/ rule above)
agent-system/extensions/literature/scripts/literature-pyenv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
